<!--
    De-vectorized reduction side effects, `option devectorize off|on`.
    Hand-written variants of the clang -O3 -fno-unroll-loops x86-64 byte sum
    (four bytes per iteration, four dword lanes, fold, remainder loop) whose
    two exits disagree on a global store at 0x3000. sum_flag stores 1 on the
    early return after the fold and 2 after the remainder loop. sum_count
    counts the remainder iterations in r9d, zeroed on both loop entries, and
    stores the count after the remainder loop only. Re-rolling either into a
    scalar loop from zero would change the stored value whenever the guard
    takes the vector arm.

    Pass 1 (`option devectorize off`) and pass 2 (`option devectorize on`)
    both keep the guard's vector arm in both functions (assertion #1) and the
    early return's store of 1 (assertion #2).

    This self-contained regression embeds 250 bytes of x86-64 code loaded at
    0x1000 and 0x1100.
-->
